---
title: Webhooks
sidebar:
  order: 1
---
Webhooks in Taskip allow your application to receive real-time HTTP notifications when specific events occur. Instead of polling the API for changes, Taskip automatically sends event data to your configured endpoint whenever a subscribed event is triggered.

This enables seamless integrations with external services, automation platforms (Zapier, Make, Activepieces, n8n), and custom backend systems.

## Access Webhook Settings

**Description:**\
The Webhook Settings page is where you can manage all webhook configurations including creation, updates, status control, and deletion.

**URL:**\
`https://app.taskip.com/settings/webhook`

**Steps to Access:**

- Log in to your Taskip workspace
- Go to **Settings** in the sidebar
- Click **Webhook**

## Create a Webhook

**Description:**\
Create a new webhook to start receiving real-time event notifications from Taskip.

**URL (UI Action):**\
`https://app.taskip.com/settings/webhook`

### Required Fields:

- **Webhook Name:** Identifier for internal use
- **Webhook URL:** Public HTTPS endpoint to receive events
- **HTTP Method:** `POST` (recommended) or `GET`
- **Custom Headers (Optional):** For authentication or metadata
- **Events:** Select which events trigger the webhook

Once saved, the webhook becomes active immediately.

## Manage Webhooks

**Description:**\
Manage existing webhooks by enabling, disabling, editing, or deleting them.

**URL:**\
`https://app.taskip.com/settings/webhook`

### Available Actions:

- **Enable/Disable:** Temporarily control delivery
- **Edit:** Update configuration fields
- **Delete:** Permanently remove webhook
- **Activity Tracking:** View last triggered timestamp

## Supported Events

**Description:**\
Taskip supports event-based triggers across multiple modules including support, forms, CRM, invoices, meetings, projects, and more.

### Support

- `support.ticket.created`
- `support.ticket.status.updated`
- `support.ticket.deleted`

### Forms

- `form.created`
- `form.submitted`

### Sales Pipeline

- `sales.pipeline.deal.created`
- `sales.pipeline.deal.stage.change`
- `sales.pipeline.deal.task.created`
- `sales.pipeline.deal.task.activity.created`
- `sales.pipeline.deal.task.meeting.created`

### Contacts & Companies

- `company.created`
- `contact.created`
- `contact.invite_to_workspace`
- `contact.join_to_workspace`

### Documents & Quotations

- `document.created`
- `document.published`
- `quotation.created`
- `quotation.status.updated`
- `quotation.sent`
- `quotation.published`

### Invoices & Payments

- `invoice.created`
- `invoice.status.update`
- `invoice.sent`
- `invoice.publish`
- `invoice.payment.paypal`
- `invoice.payment.stripe`
- `invoice.payment.mollie`
- `invoice.payment.razorpay`
- `invoice.payment.xendit`

### Meetings

- `meeting.booked`
- `meeting.cancelled`
- `meeting.rescheduled`

### Projects

- `project.created`
- `project.status.updated`
- `project.task.created`
- `project.task.status.updated`
- `project.task.comment.created`

### Discussions

- `discussion.created`

## Webhook Payload

**Description:**\
When an event is triggered, Taskip sends an HTTP request to the configured endpoint.

### Key Details:

- Content is sent via selected HTTP method
- Payload includes event name, timestamp, and related data
- Custom headers can be used for authentication

**Example Endpoint:**

```
https://your-domain.com/webhook

```

## Best Practices

**Description:**\
Follow these guidelines to ensure reliable and secure webhook integration:

- Always use **HTTPS endpoints**
- Respond with **2xx status quickly**
- Process events asynchronously
- Verify requests using headers or tokens
- Handle duplicate events safely
- Maintain logs for debugging
- Validate incoming payloads
- Secure endpoints using IP whitelist or secrets
- Test webhooks before production use

## Troubleshooting

### Webhook Not Firing

- Ensure webhook is active
- Check correct event subscription
- Verify endpoint URL is reachable

### Receiving Errors

- Ensure server returns `2xx` response
- Validate headers and payload format
- Check backend logs

### Delayed Delivery

- Ensure fast endpoint response time
- Check third-party automation tools (Zapier, Make, etc.)

## Summary

Webhooks in Taskip provide a powerful way to automate workflows and integrate external systems with real-time event delivery. Proper configuration, security practices, and monitoring ensure reliable performance across all integrations.
